    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-114033: substituting u=6x gives one-half arctan(6x)+C. q-114080: the integral is 8[arcsin(x/2)] from 0 to sqrt(3), giving 8π/3. q-162311: option 0 shows nine equally spaced points on the unit circle, including 1. q-216704: the highlighted point has angle 288°=8π/5, corresponding to k=8. q-5259: the geometric sum is 3(15^N−1)/14. q-67090: a₃=4 and r=2 imply a₁=1, so the sum is 2^N−1. q-115206: only III has an unbounded integrand on a finite integration interval; II instead has an infinite domain. q-142389 and q-82701: replace the singular lower endpoint by a and approach that endpoint from the right. q-82842: ln(2)−ln(a) tends to positive infinity as a approaches zero from the right. q-115353: substituting u=3x−2 gives the integral of u^−5 from 0 to 4, which diverges to positive infinity. q-6857: the point is (−1,−2) and the tangent slope is 6/3=2. q-122698: the tangent at (2,0) has slope π/3, so its y-intercept is (0,−2π/3). q-21081: x′=4cos(t) vanishes at π/2 and 3π/2, where y′ is nonzero. q-75288: at (−2,1), the tangent slope is −5/2 and the normal slope is 2/5. q-122898: at (0,−1), the tangent slope is 3/2 and the normal slope is −2/3. No earlier submitted answers or grades are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
